{{!-- The crop pip on a sheet's header portrait: choose which square of this face the small round
      surfaces show — the relationship rows on every sheet that lists this person, the steading
      roster, a follower card built from them.

      The same affordance the follower cards already carry, in the same visual language and the
      same corner: a small round button sitting ON the bottom-right of the picture, hidden until
      the portrait is hovered or something in it has focus, so a sheet at rest is a sheet at rest.

      Drawn in BOTH modes. Framing is not an edit-mode act — it is a reading choice about a
      picture that already exists, and the person adjusting it is usually looking at the sheet
      rather than editing it.

      Only where there is real art to frame, and only for someone who may write it — a stock icon
      or a creature-type mark has no face in it to choose a square of.

      Both pips carry .stonetop-header-pip as well as their own class: the shared one is what
      they are STYLED through (they are always styled together), their own is what the sheet
      binds its click to. --}}
{{#if canTokenize}}
{{!-- To the LEFT of the crop pip, where the vtta-tokenizer module is installed and on the same
      there-is-real-art terms as its neighbour (see headerPortraitContext): a fresh character's
      blank silhouette is not a picture to hang controls on. A SIBLING rather than something
      inside the crop dialog, because the two do different jobs and neither is a step on the way
      to the other: this one makes the pog for the map, the crop pip chooses the face for the
      sheet. Placed first so tabbing runs left to right; the visual order comes from `right` in
      the CSS, since both are absolutely positioned. --}}
<button type="button" class="stonetop-header-pip stonetop-portrait-tokenize-pip"
        data-tooltip="{{localize 'stonetop.portraitFrame.tokenizerPip'}}"
        aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.portraitFrame.tokenizerPip'}}"><i class="fas fa-circle-user"></i></button>
{{/if}}
{{#if canFrame}}
<button type="button" class="stonetop-header-pip stonetop-portrait-frame-pip"
        data-tooltip="{{localize 'stonetop.portraitFrame.pip'}}"
        aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.portraitFrame.pip'}}"><i class="fas fa-crop-simple"></i></button>
{{/if}}
